# nr-office-pdf-write-pages

mixdog-pdf: page insert/remove/copy with forms and annotations, embedded files, outline writing.

## 1. Module lines (lead-owned file)

File: native/core/crates/mixdog-pdf/src/write/mod.rs (written by nr-office-pdf-write-core).
Anchor: the module declarations after the doc comment, `pub mod info;` / `pub mod object_streams;` /
`mod serialize;` / `pub mod store;`. Add four lines so the block reads (alphabetical):

    pub mod attachments;
    pub mod copy_pages;
    pub mod info;
    pub mod object_streams;
    pub mod outline;
    pub mod pages;
    mod serialize;
    pub mod store;

No other edit to mod.rs is needed: the new files are children of `write`, so they use its private items
(`PdfDocument::pages_root`, `MAX_PAGE_TREE_DEPTH`, the `store` field) directly. The new `impl PdfDocument` blocks live in
pages.rs, copy_pages.rs, attachments.rs and outline.rs; the new public types are
`write::attachments::{AttachmentOptions, Attachment}`, `write::copy_pages::FormField` and
`write::outline::{OutlineEntry, OutlineItem}` (the twin test reaches them by these module paths; add `pub use` lines in
mod.rs only if a consumer wants them at `write::`).

## 2. Cargo / lockfile / workspace hack

None. The crate uses nothing it did not have (std, the existing `tracing`/`flate2` edges; tests use the existing
dev-dependencies mixdog-testkit and serde_json and the crate's own `flate2`).

## 3. Protocol rows, SERVICE_PENDING, compose_flip

None: this task adds library code only; no protocol method, tool or service is registered.

## 4. Fixtures

native/core/fixtures/office-write-pages/ (golden.json and its MANIFEST.json) is added with
`git add --sparse`. The recorder benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-write-pages.mjs needs the product tree
with node_modules (`--tree <tree>`) and writes the set; its helpers are recorders/lib/common.mjs (already in the tree).

## 5. Behaviour notes for the consumers (the batch operations of pdf-batch-structure.mjs, ported later)

- `PdfDocument::pages()` reads the page tree on every call, so a removal is seen at once: pdf-lib's cached page list
  that `removePageAt` invalidates by hand has no counterpart and needs no call.
- `keep_pages_in_order`, `copy_to_new_document`, `register_copied_fields`, `drop_fields_off_the_pages` are the Rust
  forms of `keepPagesInOrder`, `copyToNewDocument`, `registerCopiedFields`, `dropFieldsOffThePages`. The glue of the
  rest of the batch operations (selection of pages, rotate and crop arithmetic, merge with bookmarks, move, extract
  and attach argument handling) is written in tests/twin_write_pages.rs over these primitives and is what the batch
  port can take over.
- Like pdf-lib, `register_copied_fields` makes an empty AcroForm when the document has none (merge_pdf in Node leaves
  an empty form in a merged file whose sources have no fields).
- Attachments are embedded at once by `attach` (pdf-lib embeds at save time, so `extract_attachment` right after
  `add_attachment` in one Node batch finds nothing; here it finds the file).
